[11] The applicant in his memorandum raises the following issues:
1. Whether the Board erred in its findings concerning the practice of Christianity in China;
2. Whether the Board erred in preferring a lack of documentary evidence over the Applicant’s otherwise credible evidence;
3. Whether the Board erred by misconstruing evidence and by ignoring relevant evidence in finding that there are no incidents of arrest in Fujian Province; and
4. Whether the Board erred in relying on documentary evidence without making specific findings about the truthfulness of the Applicant’s account of events.
